' The player's side of SyncPlay: what PlayerHostView and VideoPlayerView call. Both run on the
' render thread, where an m.global read took 2.0 µs on a Stick 4K (2026-08-23, threading.md),
' so `following()` is cheap enough for a position tick. The manager is created in
' setGlobalNodes(); a test scene may have none, so every call tolerates its absence.
namespace syncPlayHooks

  ' True while this device is in a group and following its playback: the local auto-behaviors
  ' (still watching, the next-item advance, Next Episode, segment skip, Cinema Mode) stand down.
  function following() as boolean
    manager = m.global.syncPlayManager
    if not isValid(manager) then return false
    return manager.following = true
  end function

  ' Hand a player event to the manager while following. The evt shapes are SyncPlayManager.playerEvent's.
  sub notify(evt as object)
    manager = m.global.syncPlayManager
    if not isValid(manager) or manager.following <> true then return
    manager.callFunc("playerEvent", evt)
  end sub

end namespace
